The `getSettings().width` may be number or undefined; `getConstraints().width?.ideal` — width from constraints is ConstrainULong (number | ConstrainULong). Fix line 65-66: build a robust resolution getter.

Let me fix `videoSize()`: 
```ts
private videoSize(): [number, number] | null {
  const t = this.capture;
  if (!t) return null;
  const s = t.getSettings();
  const c = t.getConstraints();
  const pick = (fromSettings: number | undefined, fromConstraints: unknown): number =>
    typeof fromConstraints === 'object' && fromConstraints !== null && 'ideal' in fromConstraints
      ? (fromConstraints as { ideal?: number }).ideal ?? 1280
      : typeof fromConstraints === 'number'
        ? fromConstraints
        : fromSettings ?? 1280;
  const w = pick(s.width, c.width);
  const h = pick(s.height, c.height);
  return [w, h];
}
```

Actually simpler: MediaTrackSettings.width is `number | undefined`. Constraints width type is `ConstrainULong`. Let me just handle:

```ts
function resolve(v: number | ConstrainULong | undefined, fallback: number): number {
  if (typeof v === 'number') return v;
  if (v && typeof v === 'object' && 'ideal' in v) return v.ideal ?? fallback;
  return fallback;
}
```

ConstrainULong type available in DOM lib. Let me edit.

